{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dataset Representativeness.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dataset Representativeness.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dataset representativeness dataset representativeness","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dataset Representativeness.md","fileName":"Dataset Representativeness.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dataset Representativeness","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Data Ethics and Digital Power]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Ethics and Digital Power","Algorithmic Bias","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dataset Representativeness.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dataset Representativeness.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dataset representativeness dataset representativeness","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dataset Representativeness.md","fileName":"Dataset Representativeness.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dataset Representativeness","heading":"Dataset Representativeness","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Dataset representativeness is the degree to which data cover the people, situations, and variation relevant to a model's intended use. Size alone does not guarantee representation. A large collection can systematically omit groups, environments, or rare but consequential cases.\n\nPoor representation makes learned performance uneven and can create [[Algorithmic Bias]]. The appropriate comparison population depends on the deployment context, so a dataset suitable for one task may fail in another. Evaluating representativeness requires examining how examples were produced and selected, not only summary statistics after collection.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Ethics and Digital Power","Algorithmic Bias","aiethics.epub"],"properti